\mathcal{L}_{i+1} = \mathcal{T}_i(\mathcal{L}_i),


where $\mathcal{T}_i$ is the transformation from layer $i$ to layer $i+1$.

Theorem 13.2.3. The composite map $\mathcal{T} = \mathcal{T}_7 \circ \cdots \circ \mathcal{T}_1$ has a fixed point under compactness and continuity.

