\mathcal{A}_{t+1} = \mathcal{G}_\theta(\mathcal{A}_t, \mathcal{D}_t, \mathcal{C}),


where $\mathcal{G}_\theta$ is a generative operator.

Theorem 13.3.3. If $\mathcal{G}_\theta$ is a contraction on the space of architectures, the iteration converges to a fixed point.

Proof. Banach fixed-point theorem. $\square$

Corollary 13.3.4. Convergence depends on the architecture space being complete and $\mathcal{G}_\theta$ Lipschitz with constant $< 1$.

