Chapter 20 — Falsification Protocol

20.1 The Five Tests

Definition 20.1.1. The falsification tests S1–S5 are:

· S1: Distributed state. Can the process be represented with $x \in \mathcal{X}(\Omega)$?
· S2: Local preconditions. Can preconditions be local?
· S3: Coupled observation. Can observation and transformation be coupled?
· S4: Global viability. Is the viability kernel a subset of the full field space?
· S5: Non-degeneracy. Are the capability components non-trivial?

20.2 The Additional Tests

Definition 20.2.1. Additional tests:

· S6: Composition. Does the intermediate state remain sufficient for future compositions?
· S7: Abstraction invariance. Is the representation invariant under resolution changes?
· S8: State sufficiency–compactness. Does there exist a compact abstraction that is sufficient?

